| Severity | Count | Top Issue |
|----------|-------|-----------|
| 🔴 Critical | 0 | — |
| 🟡 Moderate | 4 | Split/LINQ allocations & linear symbol lookup on hot path |
| ℹ️ Info | 1 | Unsealed classes |

**Priority order for fixing:**
1. Finding #4 (symbol lookup) — called most frequently per string, O(n²) worst-case
2. Finding #1 (Split allocation) — array + N substrings per word-truncated string
3. Finding #2 (TrimEnd double alloc) — inconsistent with the already-optimized Left branch in the same method
4. Finding #3 (LINQ) — easy swap to span-based `string.Join`
5. Finding #5 (sealed) — mechanical, low-effort

